{"base_rate":0.45861601085481685,"brier":0.18066512890094977,"bss":0.27235472260533,"bss_hi":0.36746625032317726,"bss_lo":0.17495316749029163,"chart":{"base":[458.4,171.1],"fp":[391.4,207.4],"lead":"62,281.1 272,260.9 482,211.8 692,143.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 44% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 93% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 14%; promised 96% → rained 78%"},"rel":"78.8,403.9 346.7,273 665,130.7"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13625508819538668,"ess":336.23650486299863,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Amsterdam</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Amsterdam rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSCHELLINGWOUDE, 5.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 122 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(71&ndash;159) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>217</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>224</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Amsterdam</b> <span class=\"muted\">Netherlands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;46% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 46% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>71&ndash;159\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Amsterdam &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Amsterdam\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.14193548387097,376.96774193548384 91.512,323.76 164.94526315789474,233.5263157894737 272.4091891891892,121.29729729729729 357.0552112676056,48.76056338028167 409.4398214285714,18.0 409.4398214285714,24.5 357.0552112676056,105.15492957746477 272.4091891891892,200.0 164.94526315789474,310.1578947368421 91.512,367.44 59.14193548387097,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"215.06377204884666\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"215.06377204884666\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.14193548387097,343.4193548387097 91.512,289.78666666666663 164.94526315789474,243.10526315789474 272.4091891891892,195.0810810810811 357.0552112676056,151.2957746478873 409.4398214285714,83.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 217 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.14193548387097\" cy=\"343.4193548387097\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.512\" cy=\"289.78666666666663\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"164.94526315789474\" cy=\"243.10526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"272.4091891891892\" cy=\"195.0810810810811\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"357.0552112676056\" cy=\"151.2957746478873\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 224 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.4398214285714\" cy=\"83.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(46%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Amsterdam the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.09).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'>0.090</td><td class='num'>15.9%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.204</td><td class='num'>14.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>0.304</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.325</td><td class='num'>10.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":52.37403,"lon":4.88969,"n":737,"n_cities":216,"name":"Amsterdam","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0032258064516129037,"n":217,"obs":0.10599078341013825,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09466666666666668,"n":75,"obs":0.25333333333333335,"sig":true},{"hi":0.46,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.30210526315789477,"n":76,"obs":0.3815789473684211,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7560000000000008,"lo":0.46,"mean":0.6056756756756757,"n":74,"obs":0.5135135135135135,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.7560000000000008,"mean":0.8447887323943661,"n":71,"obs":0.6338028169014085,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9927678571428571,"n":224,"obs":0.8214285714285714,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.3,"provisional":false,"rank":122,"rank_hi":159.02499999999998,"rank_lo":71.0,"reliability":0.020386608029694386,"resolution":0.08477909982829943,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"amsterdam","station":"SCHELLINGWOUDE","timezone":"Europe/Amsterdam"}